{"id":"1dbffc89-f681-46fb-9fab-641f5b84cca0","object":"chat.completion","created":1784832113,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    nodes = case['nodes']\\n    required_symbols = set(case['required_symbols'])\\n    node_map = {n['id']: n for n in nodes}\\n    children = {n['id']: [] for n in nodes}\\n    for n in nodes:\\n        pid = n.get('parent')\\n        if pid is not None:\\n            children[pid].append(n['id'])\\n    # initial counts for required symbols\\n    counts = {sym: 0 for sym in required_symbols}\\n    for n in nodes:\\n        sym = n['symbol']\\n        if sym in required_symbols:\\n            counts[sym] += 1\\n    removed = set()\\n    removal_order = []\\n    # sort candidate nodes by (-depth, id)\\n    candidates = [n for n in nodes if n['removable'] and n['symbol'] not in required_symbols]\\n    candidates.sort(key=lambda n: (-n['depth'], n['id']))\\n    for n in candidates:\\n        nid = n['id']\\n        if nid in removed:\\n            continue\\n        # check retained children\\n        has_retained_child = any(cid not in removed for cid in children[nid])\\n        if has_retained_child:\\n            continue\\n        sym = n['symbol']\\n        # tentative removal\\n        if sym in required_symbols:\\n            counts[sym] -= 1\\n            if counts[sym] == 0:\\n                # revert\\n                counts[sym] += 1\\n                continue\\n            # else valid\\n        # else sym not required, no count change\\n        removed.add(nid)\\n        removal_order.append(nid)\\n    retained = [nid for nid in node_map if nid not in removed]\\n    retained.sort()\\n    return {'retained': retained, 'removal_order': removal_order}\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to understand the problem. The task is to implement a grammar-guided node reduction algorithm similar to Perses. The input is a tree with nodes, each 